{
  "_doc": [
    "ONE fixture, BOTH halves of the universal map gate. The browser half is",
    "acquisition.html::bskyMapGateBlock; the enforced half is public.hs_maps_map_gate_violations.",
    "They have disagreed TWICE in one day - on the key FORMAT (#560) and on the scope DEFAULT",
    "(2026-09-22) - and nothing compared them, so both shipped.",
    "",
    "EXACT PARITY IS IMPOSSIBLE BY DESIGN, and pretending otherwise is how this fixture would",
    "rot. JS recomputes the WHOLE capture key and demands equality; SQL deliberately holds no",
    "copy of the key vocabulary, because a SQL copy of a browser key rule is the drift this",
    "project keeps paying for. So SQL is necessarily the WEAKER check.",
    "",
    "THE CONTRACT IS THEREFORE DIRECTIONAL, NOT EQUAL:  sql_pass  =>  js_pass.",
    "SQL may refuse what JS allows (annoying, safe). SQL must NEVER allow what JS refuses -",
    "the dashboard is not on the path of a direct RPC call, so SQL is the only thing standing",
    "between that call and an approval.",
    "",
    "`js` and `sql` are the EXPECTED verdict of each half (true = approvable).",
    "Any case where sql=true and js=false is a SAFETY VIOLATION and must appear in",
    "known_asymmetries with a reason - an empty list is the goal, an entry is a decision.",
    "",
    "KEYS ARE DERIVED, NOT TYPED. A case whose capture_key is \"@derive\" has it computed by the",
    "SHIPPED HS.mapsCaptureKey at load time, from that case's own evidence and scope. The first",
    "draft of this fixture hand-wrote key strings and three LEGITIMATE cases failed because the",
    "invented key could not equal what the shipped rule computes - a fixture defect that reads",
    "exactly like a product defect. Only the deliberately-wrong cases carry a literal key, and",
    "each says in its name what is wrong with it.",
    "",
    "EVERY KEYED CASE ALSO CARRIES status=REAL_MAP_VISUAL, deliberately. Without it the state",
    "machine answers WAITING_CAPTURE and the gate blocks before the key is ever compared - so a",
    "key-shape case would go red for the wrong reason and prove nothing about key handling.",
    "",
    "A DATA-CENTRE-THEMED CASE ALSO CARRIES A COMPLIANT capture_policy, because mapsCaptureBound",
    "requires the MEASURED map state for that theme on top of a matching key. Without it the row",
    "is unbound for a DC-policy reason and the case would prove nothing about the universal rule."
  ],
